.TH GETRANDOM 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getrandom \- read kernel random bytes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/random.h>
.B ssize_t getrandom(void* buffer, size_t count, unsigned int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Writes at most count random bytes into the supplied buffer.
Flags are Linux getrandom flags; zero requests default behavior.
Short reads and interruptions are possible.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes read, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getrandom (2)
